    "result": "Perfect! I've successfully implemented the threshold feature for `frai eval`. Here's a summary of what was done:\n\n## Implementation Summary\n\n### Core Changes (frai-core)\n\n**1. Modified `generateReport()` function** to accept optional thresholds:\n- Added `thresholds` parameter to the function signature\n- Validates each threshold: passes if `score >= min`, fails if score is `null` or less than minimum\n- Adds two new fields to reports when thresholds are provided:\n  - `passed`: boolean indicating if all thresholds passed\n  - `thresholds`: array of `{ metric, min, score, passed }` objects\n\n**2. Updated markdown reporter** to include a \"Thresholds\" section:\n- Shows PASS/FAIL status for each threshold with min and actual scores\n- Placed before the metrics section for visibility\n\n**3. Added comprehensive test coverage** with 4 test cases:\n- Thresholds that all pass\n- Thresholds that some fail\n- Metrics with null scores (fail their thresholds)\n- Reports without thresholds (backward compatibility)\n\n### CLI Changes (frai-cli)\n\n**1. Added `--threshold` option** that can be used multiple times:\n- Format: `--threshold metric=number` (e.g., `--threshold exact_match=0.9`)\n- Can specify multiple thresholds in a single command\n\n**2. Implemented threshold parsing and validation**:\n- Validates format: must match `<metric>=<number>`\n- Validates range: value must be between 0 and 1\n- Validates metric existence: warns if metric doesn't exist in evaluations\n\n**3. Proper exit codes**:\n- **0**: Success (all thresholds passed or no thresholds specified)\n- **1**: Threshold failure (at least one threshold failed)\n- **2**: Usage error (malformed threshold or unknown metric with list of valid metrics)\n\n**4. Report always written** regardless of threshold outcome\n\n### Documentation\n\nUpdated README.md to document the new `--threshold` option with a complete description and example.\n\n### Testing Verified\n\n\u2705 Exit code 0 when all thresholds pass  \n\u2705 Exit code 1 when any threshold fails  \n\u2705 Exit code 2 for malformed thresholds and unknown metrics  \n\u2705 JSON and Markdown reports include threshold information  \n\u2705 Backward compatibility: without `--threshold` flags, behavior is unchanged  \n\u2705 Works with custom metrics via SDK  \n\nThe implementation is complete and fully backward compatible!",
